## Purpose

Make the authenticated hosted project page show durable Tool Shed work instead of becoming empty
when open counts reach zero. Preserve local Hybrid SQLite as authority while projecting a bounded,
read-only lifecycle inventory and change-only history through the existing reporter, PostgreSQL,
dashboard, and semantic SSE path.

## Desired Outcome

An operator can inspect Ideas, Project Maps, Program Roadmaps, and Campaigns; see active and
terminal states; follow Idea → Map → PRM → Campaign ownership; distinguish document lifecycle from
outcome verdict and reconciliation; identify the reporting instance and freshness; and review real
artifact transitions without one-minute duplicate rows.

## First Useful Boundary

- Freeze one versioned, privacy-bounded lifecycle snapshot and transition-event contract.
- Replace each accepted instance snapshot atomically and reject stale sequences.
- Keep per-instance truth visible and show disagreement instead of synthesizing a merged project.
- Render a filterable Work inventory and recent change-only History on the project page.
- Reuse semantic SSE invalidation so accepted lifecycle changes refresh the page and heartbeats do not.
- Qualify and deploy the complete slice through Work2, then retain formal release as a later Work5 gate.

## Workstreams

| Workstream | Outcome | Depends On |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Reporter contract | Bounded artifacts, relationships, source sequence, and change-only transitions | current Hybrid document/outcome schema |
| Hosted persistence | Atomic per-instance snapshots, retained transition history, and explicit truncation | frozen reporter contract |
| Project experience | Work and History views with filters, relationship context, freshness, and divergence | accepted hosted projection |
